# Keep the build context small and, more importantly, keep secrets out of it.
#
# Everything here would otherwise be uploaded to the daemon and be readable in
# an intermediate layer even if the final stage never copies it. `COPY . .` in
# the builder stage means an excluded file is genuinely absent, not merely
# unused.

# Secrets and keys — the reason this file exists.
keys/
*.pem
*.key
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Build artifacts: rebuilt inside the image anyway, and a stale host binary
# copied in would be silently wrong.
bin/
dist/
*.exe
*.test
*.out
coverage.*

# Version control and CI.
.git/
.github/
.githooks/
.gitattributes

# Editors and local tooling.
.vscode/
.idea/
.qwen/
.claude/

# Documentation and examples — not needed to build or run the server.
docs/architectures/
*.md
!README.md

# Local test scratch.
testdata/
